==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07~4 seconds<sup>2f~120f</sup>.
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*3 [[Samurai Doggy|Samurai Doggies]] (150%) spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 6 seconds<sup>180f</sup>.
*3 [[Samurai Doggy|Samurai Doggies]] (100%) spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*5 [[One Horn]]s spawn after 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*5 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Samurai Doggy]] (350%) spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
The enemy limit is 3, and the enemies are mostly [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies. Stacking [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cats]], [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Captain Cats]] and [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Brah Cats]] is all you need to complete this stage. The trick is to [[Knockback|knockback]] the enemies without killing them, slowly destroying the base and you won't have to deal with Bore and THE SLOTH. [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]] is almost needed if you want to deal with Bore and the Samurai Doggy stack, as they can tank the enemies while you stack [[Long Distance]] attackers to have an easier time beating the stage.

